book goblin outside guide~
Chapter 4     How A Goblin Fishes In Open Water-   The Goblin, not being
naturally inclined to sailing in large waters, ocean or a large river, must
remember that the water is not fatal.  Unlike underground waters, the current
will not drag you under a crevasse or into a rock to your death.  Therefore,
do not be afraid to fall in, as long the current is not too strong or there
aren't large rocks or crevasses to fall into.   Fish are yummy.  We have
traditionally only eaten the bottom feeders and carp that live within the
underground rivers of our homelands, but the fish of the open water are often
larger, more brightly colored, and much more flavorful.   Fish are our
friends, and our food.  A Goblin in the wild can survive for months if they
travel near a river or the ocean.  Preferably a river.  Oceans do not have too
many fish near the shore, if you are without a boat, fishing from the banks of
a river will yield more than fishing from the shore of the sea.     In bigger
waters come bigger animals, so beware! If a large predator approaches, do not
panic.  Calmly ensure the creature is aggressive or not, if the creature is
aggressive, prepare to defend your life.  If in doubt, run like hell followed
you.  A brief note about the various water bodies in the world.  The
Alden Ocean: Beware the Orca, The Great White Shark, and the Giant
Grouper.  The Giant Octopus is to be avoided as well.  The Wulftuff Ocean: The
same as above, they like to wander.   Do not board the slave galley or the
ghostly galleon, they don't take kindly to strangers.  The Tampqui River:
Avoid the darkest part of the river, the fish there are quite hungry and they
seem to see my best invis potions. Do not be afraid of Mokele, the giant
serpent.  He won't bother you if you don't bother him.  Just do not bother
him.
~
#2706
water logged book~
a water logged book~
This book is soaked but still legible.~
~
13 0 1048577
0 0 0 0
1 100 0
E
water logged book~
Tzik's Journey---

 I came here years ago, but I don't remember exactly.  I was with the
4th fleet on our journey to reinforce the beach head under Lord Zanzen.
The sail was easy and the journey was quiet, until we passed the mists.
It was the rebels, they came up on us fast.  We saw only a few ships
at first, we thought they fishing cruisers.  Then the sky went black.
We had heard stories of them, their flying ships.  We had heard that
they were powered by dark magiks and they had to be.

My ship was decimated in the first volley.  Their cannons fired iron and
magic.  I passed out and woke up here, at the end of this river.  I spent
years exploring, finding only filthy goblins and some strange half wolf
half man creatures.  I stayed in the shadows, surviving in this dark
and twisted place.  I had found a strange city, filled with bull like
creatures but they would not let me enter.  I have survived by
living off this river.  I do not think I will ever return home.  I pray
that by now, Zanzen has destroyed the ghoul menace and have
freed the people of that land from their tyranny.

I know that my time is soon to be over, the flesh eating fish have taken
most of my left leg.  I can barely walk and the jungle temperature has
made the flesh dark and foul smelling.  I hope that my wife raises our
son well.  I hope that death comes quickly to me, without pain.
I am scared.  I'm scared because I am going to die in a strange
and evil place.
~
